      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android convention for boolean setters is set/get. Amont other things, it makes kotlin\u0027s automatic property syntax work. Also elsewhere.\n\nThat said - there\u0027s an argument here for consistency with the Cronet API surface, which is already used by 1000s of apps. Helping those apps migrate to android.net.http also seems like a worthy goal. Maybe that\u0027s worth breaking with convention here?\n\nFor set/get methods like this, is it feasible to add such methods to the cronet API, on the grounds that it makes it easier for kotlin callers to use cronet?",
